On July 25, 1997 the National Assembly promulgated a decision giving the status of an autonomous college of Institute of Communications with the name ‘College of Telecommunications and Post „with headquarters in Sofia, as a university, which provides vocational training and conducts training to educational – qualification degree „ specialist in telecommunications “, with a period of study three years.
By changing the law on Higher Education in Bulgaria, educational qualification level „Specialist in communication technology “, was transformed into „Bachelor – Professional Bachelor “ (State Gazette number 41 of May 22, 2007).
Today at the University of Telecommunications and Posts are educated more than 2,100 students in the specialties:
Telecommunication Technologies;
Telecommunication Networks;
Wireless Communications and Broadcasting;
Software Engineering;
Cybersecurity of Communication Technologies
Computer Administration of Software Applications;
Management and Information Technology in Telecommunications and Post.
